Subject: [PATCH] Register runtime discovery and implement PFX file-save calls

Preserve the complete legacy WGS interface and append a distinct PFX backend.
Use an independent instance of the title-matched native PlayFab SDK for real
login, manifest synchronization, quota, conflict and upload operations.
Propagate errors and offline status; retain config handles during pending work.
Registry provider overrides are restored before returning from initialization.

Register the Gaming Services package version separately from the 64-bit GDK
interface versions. Extend large signing requests while retaining the existing
small-request IPC framing; requires the paired service patch for large bodies.

The backend runs in-process and completes a final ReleaseDeviceAsActive upload
before closing an online config. Upload after a crash/process exit and
entity-only/custom-root configs remain unimplemented. This is a qualification
candidate, not a claim of complete Gaming Services compatibility.

